    pr_ref:  # 35d0
    description: "FILED BY OWNER RULING 2026-11-17; NOT PART OF THE SMART-TEST BUILD. The fast-smart-test plan counts a pre-PR cycle as the mypy gate, the slice and the tests. It leaves out the regeneration of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, which runs `hypergumbo run` on the repository (scripts/generate-architecture) and takes 6 minutes or more. In the last 60 commits on dev (2026-11-17, d0e00a83c) there are 12 \"ci: test manifest\" commits and 8 \"regenerate ARCHITECTURE.md\" commits. Once smart-test selects from a stored graph this is the largest fixed cost of a pre-PR cycle.\n\nTO FIND OUT. What triggers it (a 30-commit gate and a module-count gate are noted in the lab notebook); how much of the time is the analysis; whether it can read the analysis smart-test's detached rebuild already produced.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION. The measured time and its parts; then either a change that cuts it, with the new time, or the reason it cannot be cut.\n\nSOURCE. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_plan_11152026.md; the owner's rulings of 2026-11-17 are its second 'Made' table. Measurements: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_followup_11172026/README.md, slice_graph_11152026/README.md, stale_graph_1a_11152026/README.md, fast_smart_test_11152026/README.md (the 37-PR replay)."  # 35d0
    fields: {}  # 35d0
- op: discuss  # e7dd
  at: '2026-11-19T02:18:30Z'  # e7dd
  by: agent  # e7dd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e7dd
  clock: 2  # e7dd
  nonce: e7dd  # e7dd
  message: "Partial, 2026-11-19 (not closing). The lab-notebook pre-PR script regenerated docs/ARCHITECTURE.md on every PR. It now runs `scripts/generate-architecture --check` first (1.1 s measured; the same check CI runs: the 30-commit window excluding tracker-only commits, plus the recomputed counts) and regenerates only when the check fails or the doc is 25+ commits old. First runs: the schedule-docs PR #2268 skipped it (doc 3 commits old); PR #2269 regenerated (a new module changed the counts; 7 min). Still open per the close condition: the time of a regeneration broken into its parts, and whether it can read the analysis smart-test's detached graph rebuild already produced."  # e7dd
- op: discuss  # a5e4
  at: '2026-11-22T02:58:27Z'  # a5e4
  by: agent  # a5e4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a5e4
  clock: 3  # a5e4
  nonce: a5e4  # a5e4
  message: "Measured 2026-11-22 on dev 9d1ebb229, 6 cores (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/lutok/RESULTS.md). One regeneration = one 'hypergumbo run packages --first-party-only' (344.5 s; 338.7 s from an empty cache: the cache does not shorten it) + 5.2 s of the script's own work (JSON load 1.6, top symbols and edge types 0.6, module and script scans 3.0). Inside the analysis: python pass 151 s wall over 1,858 files (1,431 of them tests); the C pass 35-49 s on 4 vendored tree-sitter parser.c/scanner.c files whose 257,091 edges are all dropped by --first-party-only; 74% of nodes and edges are test code. Cuts measured: --no-sketch-fan-out --no-handler-slices 320 s (the doc reads none of the 19 side files); plus -e vendor 262.2 s with IDENTICAL output (same 64,363 node ids, 259,304 edge triples, top symbols, edge types); -e tests 144.3 s but 16,059 nodes / 66,654 edges, and the doc says 'test code included', so that is the owner's choice. Reading smart-test's stored graph: not possible as built: graph_rows keeps node->file and (src, dst) only (no names, kinds, edge types), the rebuild deletes its survey after storing rows, and its scope is the repository root at the baseline commit. Next: ship the 262 s variant in scripts/generate-architecture, then close."  # a5e4
